= Psi Field =

''See: [[Psionics]]''

The '''Psi Field''' (ψ) is the effective scalar field underlying psionic phenomena — a real, measurable field that emerges from an underlying substrate rather than a fundamental field of nature, in the same sense that a crystal's phonon field or a magnet's magnetization field is real but emergent.. It is generated by coherent neural firing, focused attention, and tuned hardware; it propagates at the speed of light (or slower if it has mass); it carries energy density Ψ ≡ T<sup>00</sup>(ψ); and it couples to electromagnetism and to spacetime curvature.

This page presents the ψ field at the level of the 4D effective theory — its Lagrangian, its stress-energy tensor, the dominant interactions, and the experiential map onto practitioner sensation. For the 5D parent action see [[5D_Action_Principle]]; for the symbol reference see [[Symbol_Glossary]].

This page incorporates the content of the former '''Psi Energy Density Scalar Field''' page (which is now a redirect here). In the historical material, "Ψ" referred to the energy density of ψ — that quantity now lives in §"Energy density Ψ" below.

