== Existence condition ==

Because ψ is an [[Effective_Physics|effective field]] rather than a fundamental one, it does not exist everywhere — it '''condenses''' only where a substrate's dynamics cross a critical threshold, exactly as magnetisation appears only below the Curie temperature. The condition is derived on [[Psi Condensation Threshold|ψ-Condensation Threshold]]: the substrate must clear a bar in four structural factors — recurrence, coupling gain, coherence, and integration — combined as <math>g = R\kappa r\phi > g_c</math>. Below the bar ψ is identically zero; above it ψ condenses and its quantum, the [[Psion|psion]], acquires real mass.

Two consequences follow. First, ''organic neural tissue is the first known substrate to clear the threshold'' — the primary interface for all psionic phenomena — but it is an instance of the criterion, not its definition; recurrent, integrated systems in general are candidate substrates. Second, in the two-field treatment of the [[Effective_Field_Theory_of_Consciousness|EFT of consciousness]], the field that condenses in the first instance is the consciousness order parameter <math>C</math>, which then sources ψ; the threshold governs that <math>C</math>-condensation.

=== Emergent Effective Parameters ===

The condensation parameter

<math>
g=R\kappa r\phi
</math>

is interpreted as a macroscopic measure of substrate organization.

Because the ψ field is modeled as an emergent effective field rather than a fundamental quantum field, the macroscopic parameters appearing in the ψ field equations are expected to emerge from the substrate dynamics rather than existing as universal constants.

Accordingly, the theory treats

<math>
m_{\rm eff},
\lambda_{\rm eff},
\alpha_{\rm eff}
</math>

as effective parameters which may depend upon the substrate state.

Symbolically,

<math>
m_{\rm eff}=m_{\rm eff}(g)
</math>

<math>
\lambda_{\rm eff}=\lambda_{\rm eff}(g)
</math>

<math>
\alpha_{\rm eff}=\alpha_{\rm eff}(g)
</math>

The precise functional forms remain an open research problem and are expected to follow from a future microscopic substrate theory.

== Lagrangian density ==

The free-field Lagrangian (no EM, no source) is:

:<math>\mathcal{L}_\psi = \tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial^\mu\psi\,\partial_\mu\psi - \tfrac{1}{2} m^2 \psi^2 - \tfrac{\lambda}{4}\psi^4</math>

Adding the EM coupling and source:

:<math>\mathcal{L} = \tfrac{1}{2}\,\partial^\mu\psi\,\partial_\mu\psi - \tfrac{1}{2} m^2 \psi^2 - \tfrac{\lambda}{4}\psi^4 - \tfrac{1}{4} e^{k\psi} F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu} + J_\psi\,\psi</math>

The Euler–Lagrange equation gives the master ψ field equation on [[Psionics]]:

:<math>\Box\psi - m_{\rm eff}^2\psi - \lambda_{\rm eff}\psi^3 = \alpha_{\rm eff},F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu} + J_\psi</math>

where <math>\alpha</math> arises from the linear expansion of <math>e^{k\psi}</math>.

